me">Gotō Shinpei</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Gotō Shinpei (1857–1929) was a Japanese physician and statesman.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/goto-shojiro"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/goto-shojiro.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Goto Shojiro</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Goto Shojiro was a samurai of the Tosa domain in Japan and a leading statesman of the Meiji era.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/gottfried-heinrich-graf-zu-pappenheim"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/gottfried-heinrich-graf-zu-pappenheim.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Gottfried Heinrich Graf zu Pappenheim</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Gottfried Heinrich Graf zu Pappenheim was a Bavarian-born field marshal of the Catholic League and the Holy Roman Emperor during the Thirty Years' War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/gottfried-keller"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/gottfried-keller.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Gottfried Keller</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Gottfried Keller was a Swiss writer from Zurich and one of the major authors of German-language realism.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/gottfried-wilhelm-leibniz"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/gottfried-wilhelm-leibniz.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz was a German philosopher, mathematician and scholar.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/gotthard-kettler"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/imag